    "Task-derived event table for Aufgabenstellung Gruppe A (SS2026) — §9.4. Sources:",
    "Gruppe_A_Aufgabe_SS2026.txt network texts (shippable course handout).",
    "speedCommands: level null = the task names no speed level (e.g. NW8 'zurueckstossen',",
    "NW10 'zurueckfahren'), so any level in that direction is accepted.",
    "The STOP/restart pairs after the FIRST xR02BH3G3 halt repeat once: the halt network is",
    "level-triggered and the return move re-crosses its trigger reed — a deterministic",
    "physical consequence, not a task step.",
    "closure = n-th reedClosed (rising edge) of that reed over the whole run. NOTE: on the",
    "bouncing reed xR01D each physical crossing produces THREE rising edges, so closure #1 is",
    "the first edge of the first crossing and the crossings start at edges #1/#4/#7/#10 — the",
    "assertions here deliberately use edge #1 (the moment the PLC first sees the crossing).",
    "trailedSwitches: xW04D and xW01D are trailed twice each because A-NW7 pre-sets the",
    "Rangierfahrt route ('in Vorbereitung auf die Rangierfahrt') while the loco is still",
    "running forward over those switches — the task prescribes the trailing move. This exact",
    "multiset is load-bearing: for a switch the route only ever trails, whether it trails is",
    "the ONLY observable that constrains its §8 coilToBranch mapping (a measured mutation",
    "survey showed the reed/speed sequence alone misses A xW02BH1G1 and xW04D). xW04D's",
    "mapping is 'assumed' in trackplan.json — changing that assumption must be a deliberate",
    "edit of this table too."
  ],
